<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext HTTP is permitted for the PC and for nothing else.

  The panel talks to the PC servers over plain http on the LAN, so the listed
  hosts need an exemption, one <domain> each (ADR 0016). Granting it through a base-config instead would open
  cleartext to every address on the internet, and setting the manifest-wide
  cleartext flag on <application> does the same; both are forbidden here. See
  android/CLAUDE.md and T4.1, whose acceptance greps for precisely that mistake.

  includeSubdomains is false because this is a bare IPv4 address: an IP has no
  subdomains, and leaving the attribute at its default would widen the exemption
  past the single host it is meant to cover.

  CHANGE THIS ADDRESS to the PC's real LAN IP. 192.168.1.100 is the repository's
  agreed placeholder (T7.3), not a working address. It must match the static DHCP
  reservation for the PC — if the PC's IP moves and this file does not, the app
  reports "offline" forever and looks like a bug rather than a misconfiguration.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">192.168.1.100</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
